2>Use coroutineScope instead of withContext(EmptyCoroutineContext).
3>Use awaitAll
4>Suspending functions should be safe to call from any thread.
5>Use Dispatchers.Main.immediate instead of Dispatchers.Main.
6>Remember to use yield in heavy functions.
7>Understand that suspending functions await completion of their children.
8>Understand that Job is not inherited: it is used as a parent.
9>Don’t break structured concurrency.
10>Use SupervisorJob when creating CoroutineScope.
11>Consider cancelling scope children.
12>Before using a scope, consider under which conditions it is cancelled.
13>Don’t use GlobalScope.
14>Avoid using Job builder, except for constructing a scope.
15>Functions that return Flow should not be suspending.
16>Prefer a suspending function instead of Flow when.